@Example.AuthService_HostAddress = http://localhost:5100

GET {{Example.AuthService_HostAddress}}/weatherforecast/
Accept: application/json

###
@Example_IdentityService_HostAddress = https://localhost:7165

### Health check
GET {{Example_IdentityService_HostAddress}}/ping

### Token using ASP.NET Identity user
POST {{Example_IdentityService_HostAddress}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=example-client&client_secret=example-secret&username=admin&password=Pass123$&scope=api

### Token using client credentials
POST {{Example_IdentityService_HostAddress}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=example-client&client_secret=example-secret&scope=api

### Protected endpoint (paste access_token from either request)
GET {{Example_IdentityService_HostAddress}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
